test/check/error-primes.sumspec:10:18:
   |
10 | onSource :: App(A') -> App(A)
   |                  ^
a prime (') marks a new value, so it can only be on the target side

test/check/error-primes.sumspec:11:23:
   |
11 | twice :: App -> App(A'')
   |                       ^
a name takes at most one prime (')

test/check/error-primes.sumspec:12:33:
   |
12 | onPath :: Page.Home -> Page.Plan'
   |                                 ^
a prime (') goes only on a bare type name; a written variant or argument already says what the new value is

test/check/error-primes.sumspec:13:40:
   |
13 | onArgs :: Page.Home -> Page.Plan(A * B)'
   |                                        ^
a prime (') goes only on a bare type name; a written variant or argument already says what the new value is

